---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy — Your Resume Never Leaves Your Browser | ${BRAND}`}
  description={`${BRAND}'s keyword matcher runs 100% in your browser — nothing uploaded. The optional AI rewrite processes your text only to produce the rewrite and never stores it.`}
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Short version: we can't leak what we never receive.</p>

    <h2>The keyword matcher is 100% browser-side</h2>
    <p>
      When you paste a resume and a job description into the free matcher, the analysis runs entirely inside
      your browser using JavaScript. No text is transmitted to us or to anyone else. There is no server-side
      copy, no database, no analytics on your pasted content, and no training data. Close the tab and it's gone.
    </p>

    <h2>The optional AI rewrite is different — and says so upfront</h2>
    <p>
      The optional "Rewrite my resume for this job" feature needs a language model, so when you click it
      (it is never automatic), the resume and job description you pasted are sent to our API and processed
      by DeepSeek. We use them only to produce your rewrite and to count your free-rewrite quota
      (your account ID or a random device ID, plus token counts); we do not build profiles, sell data, or
      train models on it, and we don't store the document text.
      The free matcher above remains fully local — you never have to use the rewrite feature.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts (optional)</h2>
    <p>
      Signing in with Google is optional and unlocks account-based quota and credit packs. When you do, we
      store your Google email, display name, profile picture URL, and credit balance in our database. Your
      login session is a random token stored only as a hash — we never keep passwords (Google handles
      authentication). To delete your account data, email us and it's gone within 7 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Paid credits</h2>
    <p>
      Credit packs are one-time purchases processed by <a href="https://www.creem.io/" rel="noopener">Creem</a>,
      our Merchant of Record. Your card details go to Creem's secure checkout — we never see them. We store
      only an order record: what you bought, the amount, its payment status, and a Creem customer reference
      so refunds reach the right person.
    </p>

    <h2>What we never store</h2>
    <p>
      Your resume and job description text. The rewrite processes them in memory and keeps only a quota
      ledger — your account ID (or random device ID), the model used, and token counts. Close the tab and
      the documents themselves are gone.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this page or your data:
      <a href="mailto:support@tailorresume.dev">support@tailorresume.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
